 "context": "You are the assistant inside a small design studio's invoicing app. The person typing works at the studio. The client is Fernhill Bakery, a fictional café. You already have the studio's rate card; do not ask for it.\r\n\r\n- rate_card() -> [{\"item\":\"Website page, design and build\",\"unit\":\"page\",\"price\":650},{\"item\":\"Logo refresh\",\"unit\":\"flat\",\"price\":900},{\"item\":\"Hosting and care plan\",\"unit\":\"month\",\"price\":35},{\"item\":\"Copywriting\",\"unit\":\"page\",\"price\":120}]\r\n- terms() -> {\"upfrontDiscountPercent\":10,\"salesTaxPercent\":8,\"validDays\":30}\r\n\r\nWhat to build: an editable quote, not a static invoice. Line items live in state as an array (name, unit, qty, price). Each row has a quantity number-input and shows its line total as an expression (item.qty * item.price), never a stored copy. The rows are fixed, so the subtotal, discount, tax and total are expressions over the rows themselves (state.lines[0].qty * state.lines[0].price + ...). No set action may have an expression in its \"target\". Include copywriting as an optional line at quantity 0 the user can raise. A switch turns the upfront discount on or off. Show subtotal, discount, tax and total as currency stats. A \"Send quote\" button runs a flow: validate the total is above 0, then an \"emit\" action named \"send_quote\" carrying the lines and total, then a toast. Do not use the \"confirm\" action: this host does not allow it.",
